# Agent Design and Evaluation

COMP 4991 Independent Study, Fall 2026 · Mallory Berg · Advisor: Dr. Sean Connin

Title: *Agents and Ambiguity: Can an Agent Handle Business Intelligence Requests?*

## Status: complete (Nov 17, 2026)

The agent ran all 30 requests five times each (150 runs, Nov 13). Its runs ended
the way my answer key expected on 127 of 150, and 92 of 100 answers were acceptable after my review. The single prompt ran each request once for
comparison (Nov 14). Presented Nov 17. The final paper and deck are in the
shared folder.

Cut from the original plan: the LLM judge, the oracle run, and a second model.

## What this is

A reproducible evaluation harness that scores a deliberately simple, hand-coded agent on whether it asks, answers, or abstains correctly when given natural-language data requests against a governed, synthetic data dictionary. The harness is the product. The agent is the subject under test and stays as simple as I can keep it, so that what gets measured is the measurement itself.

The system: one hand-coded agent with a tool loop on the raw API, and a single-turn baseline that cannot ask as the control. No orchestration, no framework, no UI, no fine-tuning.



## Where things are

- `eval_v1.py` — the Inspect evaluation: runs the agent on every request five times and scores the decision.
- `tasks.jsonl` — the 30 requests with labels, scripted replies and gold SQL.
- `compare_to_gold.py` — compares each submitted answer with the gold result (AI-written; see its header).
- `system_prompt_v2.txt` — the agent's instructions for the reported run.
- `logs/` — the saved full run (`.eval`), its scored copy and the comparison files.
- `docs/methodology.md` — the outline as of Nov 7. The methodology as carried out is Appendix E of the paper.
- `compose.yaml` and `db/` — the database. `docker compose up` builds and seeds it.
- `db_sql.py` — shared read-only database connection used by both scripts.
- `baseline.py` — the single-turn control.
- `agent_v1.py` — the agent: five tools, system prompt in `system_prompt_v2.txt`, flow in `docs/agent_v1_flowchart.md`.
- `data_dictionary_v2.txt` — the dictionary both scripts read. `v0` and `v1` are kept for provenance (v0 was the baseline's original, v1 the agent's during development); no reported run uses them.
- `validation_lookup.csv` — published figures the agent checks aggregates against.

- Both scripts need a `.env` with the database connection values and an OpenRouter API key (not in the repo).
- The shared folder holds the study plan, definition of done, eval set, checkpoint documents, and status notes.


